own"}],"gloss":"ancient town","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வம்புஅணி","parts":[{"text":"வம்பு","lemma":"vampu","gloss":"new/leather strap"},{"text":"அணி","lemma":"aṇi","gloss":"adorned/wearing"}],"gloss":"newly-adorned"},{"surface":"யானை","parts":[{"text":"யானை","lemma":"yāṉai","gloss":"elephant"}],"gloss":"elephant"},{"surface":"வேந்துஅகத்","parts":[{"text":"வேந்துஅகத்","lemma":"வேந்துஅகத்","gloss":"king inside"}],"gloss":"king inside","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"துண்மையின்","parts":[{"text":"துண்மையின்","lemma":"துண்மையின்","gloss":"because of the presence"}],"gloss":"because of the presence","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நல்ல","parts":[{"text":"நல்ல","lemma":"nalla","gloss":"good/beautiful things"}],"gloss":"beautiful structures"},{"surface":"என்னாது","parts":[{"text":"என்னாது","lemma":"eṉṉātu","gloss":"without considering/not saying"}],"gloss":"without considering"},{"surface":"சிதைத்தல்","parts":[{"text":"சிதைத்தல்","lemma":"citaittal","gloss":"destroying"}],"gloss":"destroying"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வல்லையால்","parts":[{"text":"வல்லை","lemma":"vallai","gloss":"capable person"},{"text":"ஆல்","lemma":"āl","gloss":"indeed (clitic)"}],"gloss":"you are capable indeed"},{"surface":"நெடுந்தகை","parts":[{"text":"நெடுமை","lemma":"neṭumai","gloss":"great"},{"text":"தகை","lemma":"takai","gloss":"nobility/qualities"}],"gloss":"O great noble one!"},{"surface":"செருவத்","parts":[{"text":"செருவத்","lemma":"செருவத்","gloss":"in battle"}],"gloss":"in battle","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தானே","parts":[{"text":"தானே","lemma":"தானே","gloss":"indeed in"}],"gloss":"indeed in","split_unverified":true}]}],"literal":"Poison-possessing white fangs five heads borne / speedy fierce-strength serpent having entered, as if, / sky-fire to be born, having twisted, green-vined / great mountain cleft-inside thunderbolt struck like, / bird-experienced distress resolved white spear / wrath-filled army Cōḻa descendant! / Crocodiles abounding deep-placed moat, / in the wide dark pool gathering together and running, / midnight watch-keepers' torch-light reflection seizing / fiercely hostile crocodiles-having deep water reservoir's / copper-resembling fortress wall's grand ancient town, / newly-adorned elephant king inside being present, because of, / \"these are beautiful\" without saying, destroying, / you are capable indeed, O great noble one, in battle!","translation":"O descendant of the Cōḻa king who resolved the distress of the bird with his white spear and wrathful army! Like a thunderbolt that twists and strikes inside the cleft of a great mountain covered with green vines, causing fire to erupt in the sky as if a speedy, fiercely strong five-headed serpent with white fangs of poison had entered it, you strike. Because the enemy king with newly-adorned elephants is inside, you destroy without sparing, saying 'these are beautiful,' the grand ancient town with copper-like fortress walls and a deep-water moat filled with fiercely hostile crocodiles that gather and run in the wide, dark depths, snatching even the reflection of the torches held by the midnight watchmen. You are indeed capable of such destruction in battle, O great noble one!","modern":"விஷப் பற்களையும் ஐந்து தலைகளையும் கொண்ட வேகமும் வலிமையும் மிக்க பாம்பு நுழைந்தது போல, வானத்தில் நெருப்புப் பொறி பறக்க, பசிய கொடிகள் படர்ந்த பெரிய மலையின் பிளவுக்குள் இடி விழுந்தது போல நீ தாக்குகிறாய். பறவையின் (புறாவின்) துன்பத்தைத் தீர்த்த சிபிச் சக்கரவர்த்தியின் வழியில் வந்த, ஒளிவீசும் வேலையும் சினமிக்க படையையும் உடைய செம்பியனே! அகன்ற இருண்ட நீரில் கூட்டமாக ஓடி, நள்ளிரவில் காவல் காப்போரின் தீவட்டி வெளிச்சத்தின் நிழலைக் கவ்வி இழுக்கும் கொடிய முதலைகளைக் கொண்ட ஆழமான அகழியையும், செம்பைப் போன்ற மதில்களையும் உடையது அந்தப் பழமையான பெருமைமிக்க ஊர். புதிய அணிகலன்களை அணிந்த யானைகளைக் கொண்ட பகை வேந்தன் அவ்வூரின் உள்ளே இருக்கிறான் என்ற ஒரே காரணத்திற்காக, 'இவை அழகானவை' என்று பாராமல் அவற்றை அழிப்பதில் வல்லவனாக இருக்கிறாய், பெருந்தகையே!","explanation":"The poet Māṟōkkattu Nappacalaiyār addresses the Cōḻa king Kuḷamuṟṟattu-tuñciya Kiḷḷi Vaḷavaṉ, praising his fierce military prowess. The poem belongs to the vākai (victory) or uḻiñai (siege) tiṇai, describing the relentless destruction of an enemy's fortified town. The poet compares the king's assault to a terrifying thunderbolt striking a mountain cleft, evoking the image of a venomous five-headed serpent. The description of the moat is exceptionally vivid, noting that the crocodiles are so aggressive they snap at the mere reflections of the torches held by the night watchmen. Despite the beauty and antiquity of the copper-walled fortress, the king destroys it without hesitation because his enemy is inside. Key phrases include 'புள்ளுறு புன்கண் தீர்த்த' referring to the legendary ancestor Sibi, and 'சிதைத்தல் வல்லையால்' highlighting the king's destructive capability in war.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,1.0],[1.0,1.3],[1.3,1.6],[1.6,1.9],[1.9,2.6],[2.6,2.8],[2.8,3.1],[3.1,3.4],[3.4,4.54],[4.54,4.7],[4.7,4.7],[4.7,6.1],[6.1,7.2],[7.2,7.7],[7.78,8.3],[8.3,8.7],[8.7,9.6],[9.6,9.6],[9.6,10.4],[10.4,10.6],[10.6,10.9],[10.9,11.9],[11.9,12.6],[12.6,12.8],[12.8,13.3],[13.3,13.52],[13.52,14.6],[14.6,14.8],[14.8,15.2],[15.2,16.54],[16.54,17.0],[17.0,17.7],[17.7,18.0],[18.68,19.28],[19.28,19.38],[19.38,20.58],[20.58,21.01],[21.01,21.08],[21.08,22.68],[22.68,22.78],[22.92,23.78],[23.78,24.88],[24.88,25.08],[25.08,25.98],[25.98,26.38],[26.38,27.38],[27.38,27.78],[27.78,28.38],[28.38,28.98],[28.98,29.68],[29.68,30.28],[30.28,30.58],[30.58,31.98],[31.98,32.58],[32.58,32.75],[32.84,33.18]],"female":[[0.0,0.7],[0.8,1.0],[1.0,1.3],[1.3,1.8],[1.8,2.1],[2.1,3.1],[3.1,3.3],[3.3,3.7],[3.7,4.0],[4.0,5.5],[5.5,6.38],[6.38,6.5],[6.5,7.3],[7.3,8.5],[8.5,9.1],[9.17,9.7],[9.7,10.63],[10.63,10.81],[10.81,11.68],[12.1,12.2],[12.3,12.4],[12.5,12.7],[12.7,13.7],[13.7,14.3],[14.3,14.5],[14.5,15.0],[15.0,15.8],[15.8,16.4],[16.4,16.6],[16.6,17.0],[17.0,17.5],[17.5,18.5],[18.5,19.